A1. How good girls get home. ~ WALK
A4. This bird is always kidding some one. ~ STORK
A8. An asinine objection. ~ BALK
A12. If you had this you'd be angry. ~ IRE
A13. A holy fright—in fact it's awful. ~ AWE
A14. He's always looking for his honey. ~ BEE
A15. The first evening gown. ~ LEAF
A17. How Tired Business Men do not spend their evenings. ~ SLEEP
A19. Kind of woman who never talks about her neighbors. ~ MUTE
A20. Pirate's promenade. ~ PLANK
A22. When girls are always coming out. ~ DEBUT
A24. Hard drink. (Prohibition.) ~ ICE
A25. This is over the head of the Scotch. ~ TAM
A27. This measures up well—if it's in good condition. ~ METER
A29. Makers of divine music. ~ HARPS
A32. An ill-mannered fellow. ~ BOOR
A34. Amatory obstacle. ~ RIVAL
A36. One woman would make this impossible. ~ STAG
A38. Last words of a bachelor. ~ IDO
A39. An exclamation. ~ GAD
A40. Slick stuff. ~ OIL
A41. Married men's retreat. ~ DENS
A43. These are intoxicating. ~ WINES
A45. Painful. ~ SORE
A46. A fox-hunter's hobby. ~ STEED
A48. This is hell for a Hebrew. ~ SHEOL
A50. How Coolidge got to Washington. ~ RAN
A51. This is epochal. ~ ERA
A53. What Miss Muffet was eating. ~ CURDS
A55. Oozes slowly. ~ SEEPS
A58. Just a little bit—you can't see this. ~ ATOM
A60. A letter carrier. ~ STAMP
A62. A soft place. ~ SOFA
A64. That large Australian bird. ~ MOA
A65. What women never tell. ~ AGE
A66. Roman household God. ~ LAR
A67. A pugilistic present. ~ BELT
A68. What Mr. White got at Palm Beach. ~ BROWN
A69. This is always stopping liquor. ~ CORK

D1. What Prohibition makes us. ~ WILD
D2. Part of the verb to be. ~ ARE
D3. A hop-off. ~ LEAP
D5. The result of conversation. ~ TALK
D6. What you do when you're in debt. ~ OWE
D7. Vocal cords of a saxophone. ~ REED
D9. To be next to. ~ ABUT
D10. What landlords do. ~ LET
D11. To have and to hold. ~ KEEP
D16. This man is always getting up in the air. ~ FLIER
D17. A villainous expression. ~ SNEER
D18. This is attached to flowers. ~ PETAL
D19. A swell affair. ~ MUMPS
D21. What actors should learn to do. ~ ACT
D23. The drinks are often on this. ~ BAR
D26. What mother-in-laws usually do. ~ ABIDE
D27. Love-light (pl.). ~ MOONS
D28. A little stiff—or a big one. ~ RIGID
D29. This is Hell. ~ HADES
D30. A police pigeon. ~ STOOL
D31. What the sheik does when Sheba passes. ~ OGLES
D33. A poem. ~ ODE
D35. This is always moving. ~ VAN
D37. What aviators go up in. ~ AIR
D42. Try this on your ukulele. ~ STRUM
D43. Makes his way; travels. ~ WENDS
D44. This is all woolly. ~ SHEEP
D45. These are used in a clean-up. ~ SOAPS
D47. Use this when you listen-in. ~ EAR
D49. Before. ~ ERE
D52. Only a sheep can have this. ~ LAMB
D53. Found in the best cellars. ~ COAL
D54. This is always acting up. ~ STAR
D55. A diving duck-like bird. ~ SMEW
D56. A single outrage. ~ SOLO
D57. This covers the prettiest limbs. ~ BARK
D59. Pedal digit. ~ TOE
D61. Past. ~ AGO
D63. Distant. ~ FAR


